# Frontend environment variables (Vite).
#
# The frontend reads these at build time (production) or dev-server start
# (local). To override the defaults below, copy this file:
#
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env.local
#
# Vite loads .env, .env.local, .env.development, .env.production in that
# order. `.env.local` is git-ignored and the right choice for personal
# overrides. `./scripts/numio-dev.sh run frontend` does not require any of
# these to be set — the defaults below are enough for the bypass-mode flow.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API base URL — optional in bypass mode, optional in Cognito mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Leave empty (the default). When empty, the frontend issues relative
# requests to `/api/...`, which the Vite dev server proxies to the backend
# (see frontend/vite.config.js -> server.proxy). The proxy target is set by
# numio-dev.sh via BACKEND_PROXY_TARGET.
#
# Set this only if you are serving the frontend against a backend on a
# different origin (e.g. a deployed preview). Example:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.preview.numio.ai
# VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API mode — mock or real data source for the whole app (build-time)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Allowed values: mock | real.  Default: real.
#
# - real (default): the app talks to the backend through the API layer.
# - mock: the app runs end-to-end from generated synthetic data with no
#   backend, no database, and no AWS connectivity — for a standalone demo and
#   for deterministic Vitest/Puppeteer tests.
#
# This file is DOCUMENTATION ONLY for this variable. Vite does not load
# .env.example, and the build default is set by the `define` block in
# frontend/vite.config.js (an unset value compiles to "real"). Select mock mode
# per-command, not by editing this file — prefer the numio-dev.sh flag:
#   ./scripts/numio-dev.sh run frontend --mock   # backend-free demo (dev server)
#   VITE_API_MODE=mock npm run build             # one-off static demo bundle
# See docs/frontend/mock-backend-spec.md and the "Frontend mock mode" section
# of docs/dev-runbook.md.
# VITE_API_MODE=real

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cognito — required only when AUTH_ENABLED=true on the backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Local dev default is AUTH_ENABLED=false on the backend; in that mode the
# Login page is never reached and none of the three VITE_COGNITO_* vars are
# needed.
#
# If you flip AUTH_ENABLED=true, fill in all three. Obtain the values from
# the Cognito user pool and app client you have been assigned.

# Cognito hosted-UI domain (no trailing slash).
#   Example: https://numio-dev.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=

# Cognito app client ID.
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth redirect URI registered with the Cognito app client.
# Defaults to `${window.location.origin}/login` when unset, which matches
# `http://localhost:5173/login` for the standard dev setup.
# VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI=
